    "summary": "- Invite tokens are 32 random bytes from crypto/rand in unpadded base64url. Only the SHA-256 hash is stored, and the token appears only in the invitation email. No POST or GET response and no snapshot contains it.\n- POST /v1/invites/accept returns 404 `invite_not_found`, 410 `invite_used`, or 410 `invite_expired` (more than 7 days after creation, on the service clock). Re-inviting an address (case-insensitive) revokes the old invite, so only the newest token works.\n- GET /v1/invites lists only pending invites, each with `expires_at`. Tests cover each rule, and `go build ./...`, `go test ./...`\n...[truncated]",
